+</p>
+
+You get one attempt at the Optiver online assessment every eight months. OptPrep lets you sit it as many times as you like first: timed practice, worked lessons and recent-question tracking. Formats are practice assumptions except where a current invitation confirms them; practice targets have not been validated against Optiver results.
+
+## Run this copy
+
+1. Extract the archive into a folder.
+2. Open a terminal in that folder.
+3. With Node.js 20 or newer installed, run:
+
+```bash
+npm start
+```
+
+No npm installation is needed for the app. The local address is normally http://127.0.0.1:8765. The launcher opens the browser automatically; run `node bin/optprep.js --no-open` to keep it manual.
+
+Alternatively, with Python 3.10 or newer, run `python serve.py`. That starts the optional local backend as well.
+
+Select **Career Kickstarter: Trading**. Its BTO practice has both a 25-minute total cap and a 90-second item cap. The item count and item cap are practice assumptions; the overall 25-minute cap follows the 2027 invitation. Full mocks use only the selected battery.
+
+To move existing progress from the original site, export a backup in its Settings and import it into this copy. Exam history, lessons and XP are preserved. Old Intervals skill levels are reassessed because they did not require useful interval scores. Fresh-question tracking starts with questions viewed in this edition.
+
+The upstream site and `npx optprep` run the original release; use the commands above to run these fixes.
+
+## What you practise
+
+Pick the battery you will sit, and OptPrep matches the tasks and clocks to it.
+
+| Battery | Tasks |
+|---|---|
+| Career Kickstarter: Trading | Beat the Odds, NumberLogic, Likelihood List, Intervals (45 s each), Orderbooks, Zap-N |
+| Trader and Quant Trader | 80-in-8, NumberLogic (15 in 25 min), Beat the Odds (30 questions), Likelihood List, Zap-N |
+| Everything | Every task at its most commonly reported format |
+
+| Task | Exam replica | Scoring |
+|---|---|---|
+| 80-in-8 | 80 questions in 8 minutes, tap to answer, no going back | +1 right, −1 wrong |
+| Beat the Odds | Kickstarter: 20 practice questions, 90 s each, 25 min overall | +1, −1, or skip for 0 |
+| NumberLogic | 26 sequences in 25 minutes, skip and return | +1, −1, or skip for 0 |
+| Likelihood List | 15 sets of three statements, 90 s each | 1 point for the exact order |
+| Intervals | 18 estimates, 60 s each | lower ÷ upper when the truth is inside |
+| Orderbooks | 20 boards in 8 minutes | boards solved; a wrong submit costs 5 s |
+| Zap-N | 9 games | each scored against the best possible play |
+
+After the online assessment, Optiver's interviews include market-making games. OptPrep's bonus round has you quote two-sided markets against a trader who knows more than you.
+
